# vpdemo: the Viewport widget driving Tea v2 under a real pty (S4).
#
# The demo renders a live header "off=<yOffset> size=<cols>x<rows>" above the
# viewport (40 numbered rows), so every scroll state has a UNIQUE needle.  The
# first paint is the startup resize probe at the pty default 80x24:
#   \e[?25l \e[2Koff=0 size=80x24\r\n \e[2Krow-00…\r\n … (24 rows)
# Every directive is settled by an expect BEFORE the next fires (lgdemo
# discipline).  j/k scroll a line, \e[6~ = pgdn pages by the height (24 ->
# clamped to maxYOffset 16), `resize 40 12` re-renders at the new dims, and
# the SGR wheel-up packet scrolls by the 3-line delta.  q quits via the
# TaskQuit scan (show cursor + exit 0).
expect \e[?25l\e[2Koff=0 size=80x24
send j
expect off=1 size=80x24
send j
expect off=2 size=80x24
send \e[6~
expect off=16 size=80x24
send k
expect off=15 size=80x24
resize 40 12
expect off=15 size=40x12
send \e[<64;5;3M
expect off=12 size=40x12
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
